{
  "id": "7-eleven-pokemon-fair",
  "name": "7-Eleven Pokémon Fair",
  "category": "retailer_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "7-Eleven stores in Japan gave a sealed pack with a bottle of Coca-Cola Vanilla, Sprite Classic, Ambasa Sour White, Fanta Fruit Punch or Fanta Melon Soda in their Pokémon Fair, which began on 25 June 2003 and lasted until the packs ran out. The packs advertised the sixth Pokémon film, Jirachi: Wish Maker. Twenty-one cards came in them, ADV-P 015 to 035: ten Pokémon in both non-holo and cosmos holofoil, from Treecko, Torchic and Mudkip to Groudon, Flygon and Absol, and a secret eleventh, Jirachi, only in cosmos holofoil. Every card carries a 7-Eleven stamp in its bottom left corner. Most of the art came out in English, without the stamp, as Nintendo Black Star Promos.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: 7-Eleven Pokémon Fair campaign",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/7-eleven-pokemon-fair-campaign/"
      },
